{"content_hash": "58a4b143fdca9e45", "version_id": 127, "article_id": 13, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "ケイン選手、イングランドで125試合目の記録を作る", "title_zh": "凯恩迎来英格兰第125场比赛，创下新纪录", "topic": "sports", "source": "skysports", "source_url": "https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12040/13595959/harry-kane-breaks-england-appearance-record-but-can-he-take-that-final-step-to-complete-his-career", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://e0.365dm.com/26/10/1920x1080/skysports-kane-england_7370090.jpg?20261006225617", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 329, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "ハリー・ケイン選手はイングランド代表として125試合に出ました。チェコ戦で2ゴールと1アシストをしました。でも、まだ大きなトロフィーがありません。", "lead_zh": "哈里·凯恩为英格兰队出场125次。在对捷克的比赛中他进了两球，还有一次助攻。但他还没有拿到重要奖杯。", "preview": "ハリー・ケイン選手はイングランド代表として125試合に出ました。これはピーター・シルトン選手と同じ記録です。チェコとの試合で、ケイン選手は2ゴールと1アシストをしました。イングランドは3対0で勝ちました。", "preview_zh": "哈里·凯恩为英格兰队出场125次。这和彼得·希尔顿的纪录一样。在对捷克的比赛中，凯恩进了两球，还有一次助攻。英格兰3比0获胜。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 117, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/audio/13/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 70.275, "size_bytes": 425376, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 213, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/data/versions/127.json", "paragraphs": ["ハリー・ケイン選手はイングランド代表として125試合に出ました。これはピーター・シルトン選手と同じ記録です。チェコとの試合で、ケイン選手は2ゴールと1アシストをしました。イングランドは3対0で勝ちました。", "ケイン選手は「自分の夢を超えています。125試合はとても光栄です」と言いました。彼は21歳で代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手より遅いスタートでした。", "ケイン選手はいつも試合に出ています。この10年で、出られなかった試合は1つだけです。彼は「痛みがあっても試合に出ます。出られることは一番の強みです」と言いました。", "しかし、ケイン選手にはまだ大きなトロフィーがありません。彼は「記録より、イングランドで何か勝ちたいです」と言いました。まだ32歳です。これからももっと上手になると思います。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["哈里·凯恩为英格兰队出场125次。这和彼得·希尔顿的纪录一样。在对捷克的比赛中，凯恩进了两球，还有一次助攻。英格兰3比0获胜。", "凯恩说：“这超出了我的梦想。125场是非常光荣的。”他21岁首次代表国家队出场。比韦恩·鲁尼和迈克尔·欧文起步晚。", "凯恩总是上场比赛。这十年里，他只有一场不能上场。他说：“即使疼我也会上场。能上场是最大的优势。”", "但是，凯恩还没有重要奖杯。他说：“比起纪录，我更想和英格兰一起赢点什么。”他只有32岁。我觉得他还会变得更强。"], "body": "ハリー・ケイン選手はイングランド代表として125試合に出ました。これはピーター・シルトン選手と同じ記録です。チェコとの試合で、ケイン選手は2ゴールと1アシストをしました。イングランドは3対0で勝ちました。\n\nケイン選手は「自分の夢を超えています。125試合はとても光栄です」と言いました。彼は21歳で代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手より遅いスタートでした。\n\nケイン選手はいつも試合に出ています。この10年で、出られなかった試合は1つだけです。彼は「痛みがあっても試合に出ます。出られることは一番の強みです」と言いました。\n\nしかし、ケイン選手にはまだ大きなトロフィーがありません。彼は「記録より、イングランドで何か勝ちたいです」と言いました。まだ32歳です。これからももっと上手になると思います。", "body_zh": "哈里·凯恩为英格兰队出场125次。这和彼得·希尔顿的纪录一样。在对捷克的比赛中，凯恩进了两球，还有一次助攻。英格兰3比0获胜。\n\n凯恩说：“这超出了我的梦想。125场是非常光荣的。”他21岁首次代表国家队出场。比韦恩·鲁尼和迈克尔·欧文起步晚。\n\n凯恩总是上场比赛。这十年里，他只有一场不能上场。他说：“即使疼我也会上场。能上场是最大的优势。”\n\n但是，凯恩还没有重要奖杯。他说：“比起纪录，我更想和英格兰一起赢点什么。”他只有32岁。我觉得他还会变得更强。", "text": "ハリー・ケイン選手はイングランド代表として125試合に出ました。これはピーター・シルトン選手と同じ記録です。チェコとの試合で、ケイン選手は2ゴールと1アシストをしました。イングランドは3対0で勝ちました。 ケイン選手は「自分の夢を超えています。125試合はとても光栄です」と言いました。彼は21歳で代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手より遅いスタートでした。 ケイン選手はいつも試合に出ています。この10年で、出られなかった試合は1つだけです。彼は「痛みがあっても試合に出ます。出られることは一番の強みです」と言いました。 しかし、ケイン選手にはまだ大きなトロフィーがありません。彼は「記録より、イングランドで何か勝ちたいです」と言いました。まだ32歳です。これからももっと上手になると思います。", "vocab": [{"word": "試合", "pos": "noun", "zh": "比赛", "note": "常用词，指体育比赛"}, {"word": "代表", "pos": "noun", "zh": "代表（国家队）", "note": "常指国家队"}, {"word": "記録", "pos": "noun", "zh": "纪录", "note": "如“记录”"}, {"word": "ゴール", "pos": "noun", "zh": "进球", "note": "外来语"}, {"word": "アシスト", "pos": "noun", "zh": "助攻", "note": "外来语"}, {"word": "トロフィー", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奖杯", "note": "外来语"}, {"word": "デビュー", "pos": "noun", "zh": "首次出场", "note": "外来语，指初次登台"}, {"word": "光栄", "pos": "adj", "zh": "光荣", "note": "形容非常荣幸"}, {"word": "強み", "pos": "noun", "zh": "优势", "note": "长处、强项"}, {"word": "痛み", "pos": "noun", "zh": "疼痛", "note": "身体上的痛"}], "title_original": "Kane sums up England legacy on special night - but can he make that final step?", "summary_original": "Some things are inevitable in life. Harry Kane delivering for England is always one of those inevitabilities. On his momentous, milestone match, he stuck to the script perfectly.", "body_original": "Analysis\nHarry Kane breaks England appearance record but can he take that final step to complete his career?\nHarry Kane got two goals and an assist on his 125th cap for England in the 3-0 win over the Czech Republic; the England captain is now level with Peter Shilton at the top of the Three Lions' all-time appearance list - but Kane still needs that trophy to be the undisputed best\nSam Blitz\nFootball Journalist\n@SamBIitz\nTuesday 6 October 2026 23:22, UK\nPlease use Chrome browser for a more accessible video player\nSome things are inevitable in life. Harry Kane delivering for England is always one of those inevitabilities. On his momentous, milestone match, he stuck to the script perfectly.\nOn his 125th cap, Kane did what Kane does best under the Wembley arch - stealing the show, leading the way, winning the game for England.\nEveryone knew he would score in this match. It's the same feeling you get in\nevery\nmatch. But he still gets the buzz.\nEngland 3-0 Czech Republic - report and reaction\nWho are the winners and losers of this England camp?\n\"I think this is even beyond my wildest dreams,\" he said after the game. \"To be now at 125, it's just an extreme privilege.\"\nThis match - and the three goals he contributed to England's cause on his special night - was a perfect summary of Harry Kane's England career.\nThe first goal saw him venture out to the right wing, highlighting Kane's ability to pop up anywhere on the pitch. Quarterback, out wide, it doesn't matter. It's classic Kane.\nBut his two goals were classic centre-forward strikes. Right in the heart of the penalty area, almost a throwback to the classic No 9.\n\"He's playing at a level that is unmatched,\" said Jude Bellingham on Kane's record-breaking night. \"He's scoring goals for fun, he's dropping deep and playing passes in behind and contributing, making tackles and everything. He's only getting better.\"\nWhat makes Kane's achievement even more incredible is he has reached 125 caps despite making his England debut at 21. For a generational talent in the modern game, that's somewhat rare. Bellingham, for example, was 17 when he played his first game.\nKane did not have the teenage sensation moment Wayne Rooney or Micheal Owen had. Bukayo Saka and Rio Ferdinand were also 19 on their England debuts. Declan Rice and Phil Foden were 20. Kane was the slow starter who forged his way up through the EFL and became a national hero.\nMonterosa\nThis content is provided by\nMonterosa\n, which may be using cookies and other technologies.\nTo show you this content, we need your permission to use cookies.\nYou can use the buttons below to amend your preferences to enable\nMonterosa\ncookies or to allow those cookies just once.\nYou can change your settings at any time via the\nPrivacy Options\n.\nUnfortunately we have been unable to verify if you have consented to\nMonterosa\ncookies.\nTo view this content you can use the button below to allow\nMonterosa\ncookies for this session only.\nEnable Cookies\nAllow Cookies Once\nAnd what has followed is 125 caps in 11 years. The remarkable consistency is summarised by his availability. He's always there for England.\nIn England's last 101 competitive matches - which spans a decade - Kane has been available for selection for all but one of them: the Nations League loss to Greece in 2024.\nEvery single other game, he has been able to be called upon for the Three Lions. A century of near-perfectly consistent England performances over the span of a decade.\n\"For sure there's times I've played through the pain\", he said. \"I think every player at some stage plays through the pain or niggles or some sort of injury.\n\"I think the last six years or so I've been extremely consistent in that sense and been available. I think availability is one of the biggest strengths you can have at this level.\"\nNow it's important to recognise that Kane hasn't always been 100 per cent fit in those 100 matches. The Euro 2024 campaign and final spring to mind where he was clearly carrying something but playing through the pain.\nBut his predecessor at the England elite level in Rooney was riddled with injury sagas through his career - Euro 2004 and the 2006 World Cup especially.\nThe main image of his 2010 World Cup highlight reel was him shouting down the TV cameras to England fans, then he faded out of form in 2012, 2014 and 2016 - to the point where he was no longer the main man. Kane has shown the consistency Rooney never could.\nNow Rooney, Owen and Co were part of a different generation where playing for England was not as attractive as it is now. Turning up regularly for international duty was not as common, with the 'club first culture' well-documented on many levels.\nBut then again, Kane's big night came on the same evening that Cristiano Ronaldo revealed his reasons for leaving the Portugal camp. Even the very best can easily turn away from the national team for any reason. Kane has never even given a glimmer of that attitude in his 11 years.\n\"To reach the highest level on a consistent basis you've always got to be hungry, you've always got to be striving for more,\" he said.\n\"I think sometimes players or people can reach the top and think it's time to take their foot off the gas and that's when you see players maybe fall.\n\"For me it's the opposite. When I'm at the top it's to do even more, find even more improvement. That's what I'm doing right now.\"\nKane is the exemplary player England needed for this generation - but all that remains is for him to confirm his place as the greatest player in\nany\ngeneration.\nIs he already England's best? Quite possibly. Record appearance maker and goalscorer is hard to top and argue against. But the one thing Ronaldo, Bobby Charlton and Bobby Moore have over him is silverware at international level. \"For sure I'd swap all [the caps and goals] to win something with England.\"\nBut Kane also said: \"Every player has a ceiling.\" What is his? Has he already reached it? \"I hope not. I hope there's still more to go. I guess only time dictates that, where everyone's ceiling is.\n\"Right now I still feel like I've got room to improve. I just said that I've come off the back of my best season ever at 32 years old and right now I feel even in a better place.\"\nThere is still plenty for him to get. Kane is first eyeing up 100 goals at international level, joining a very elite club of strikers to manage that feat. He will surely get there.\n\"I try not to think about it too much,\" he said, with a sense of humility. \"It's like being a cricketer in the 90s, the more you think about the 100, you don't know where to get there.\nBut in this all-time great innings - as well as the upcoming Ballon D'Or trophy, which he surely has more than half a chance for - delivering a first major international trophy since 1966 is the ultimate prize.\nKane has at least one more bite at the trophy cherry. He looks set to appear at Euro 2028 and possibly he can squeeze out one last crack at the World Cup, following this summer's disappointment.\n\"I'm in great shape,\" he said. \"Some of the players I've played with went into their late 30s and are still at the highest level and are even in their 40s now. It's season by season with me.\n\"As long as I feel like I can help the team and be valuable for the team I'll be around. At the moment I feel like I can't help the team, I won't and that's the way I am. We'll have to see.\"\nFor now, one message stands with Kane. \"Don't give yourself any regrets.\" He has done so much - but it's time for the last, big challenge. Win it all. Win what remains.\nAround Sky\nUpgrade to get all of Sky Sports, including 1500 live football matches this season\nNot got Sky? Get instant access to Sky Sports with no contract", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:54:02.318992", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "ハリー", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.613, "sm": 125, "em": 612, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "・", "s": 0.613, "e": 0.83